   $q$How does the author connect the mild winter of 1890 to the rise of ice machines?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The machines warmed the region's climate, which caused the lake ice to grow too thin.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"The thin lake ice left cities short, so they turned to machines that made ice with steam.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The machines were invented in Wexmoor to help the icehouses last through a warm summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The mild winter let Wexmoor build machines because workers no longer had to cut ice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The thin lake ice left cities short, so they turned to machines that made ice with steam.$q$, $q$Paragraph 4 says the mild season left the ice too thin to cut, and "the cities, short of ice, turned to" the steam machines. The weather caused the shortage; the machines did not cause the weather.$q$, 'draft', '95f8d987-0aa8-5210-8647-ad01bca73e0d')
